      question: "What is the standard passport photo size worldwide?",
      answer: "There is no single worldwide standard. The most common size is 35mm × 45mm, used by India, UK, most European countries, and Australia. The USA uses 2 inches × 2 inches (51mm × 51mm). Canada uses 50mm × 70mm. Always check your specific country's requirements.",
    },
    {
      question: "Can I use the same passport photo for different countries?",
      answer: "No. Each country has specific size, background, and file size requirements. A photo formatted for an Indian passport won't meet US requirements. Always use your country's specific dimensions when preparing passport photos.",
    },
    {
      question: "What file format and size do I need for passport photos?",
      answer: "Most countries require JPEG format. File size limits vary: India requires 10-50KB, USA allows up to 600KB, UK allows up to 10MB, and Canada allows up to 4MB. Digital submissions often have different limits than printed photos.",
    },
    {
      question: "What background color is required for passport photos?",
      answer: "Most countries require a plain white background. Some accept light grey or off-white. The USA, India, and most European countries require white. The UK accepts both grey and white. Never use colored, patterned, or gradient backgrounds.",
    },
  ]}
