        <h2>Common Requirements Across All Countries</h2>
        <p>While dimensions vary, most countries share these requirements:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Face must be centered</strong> — Take up 70-80% of the photo area</li>
          <li><strong>Neutral expression</strong> — Mouth closed, no smiling for some countries</li>
          <li><strong>Open eyes</strong> — Looking directly at the camera</li>
          <li><strong>No headwear</strong> — Unless for religious reasons (with documentation)</li>
          <li><strong>No glasses</strong> — Many countries now require glasses to be removed</li>
          <li><strong>Recent photo</strong> — Taken within the last 6 months</li>
          <li><strong>No filters</strong> — No beauty filters, color adjustments, or retouching</li>
          <li><strong>Even lighting</strong> — No harsh shadows on face or background</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>India-Specific Requirements</h2>
        <p>Indian passport photos have strict requirements that differ from most other countries:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Size:</strong> 35mm × 45mm (3.5cm × 4.5cm)</li>
          <li><strong>Pixels:</strong> 413 × 531 at 300 DPI</li>
          <li><strong>File Size:</strong> 10KB to 50KB (JPG format)</li>
          <li><strong>Background:</strong> Plain white</li>
          <li><strong>Expression:</strong> Neutral, mouth closed</li>
          <li><strong>Eyes:</strong> Open, looking directly at camera</li>
        </ul>
        <p>For Indian government forms, file size requirements vary:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>SSC CGL/CHSL:</strong> 20-50KB</li>
          <li><strong>UPSC Civil Services:</strong> 20-50KB</li>
          <li><strong>Aadhar Card:</strong> Up to 300KB</li>
          <li><strong>PAN Card:</strong> Up to 200KB</li>
          <li><strong>Bank Account:</strong> 20-50KB</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How to Create Passport Photos Online</h2>
        <p>Creating a passport photo that meets all requirements is straightforward:</p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Take a photo</strong> — Use natural lighting, white background, face the camera directly from 1-2 meters away</li>
          <li><strong>Use our tool</strong> — Visit <a href="/passport-photo-size">our passport photo tool</a></li>
          <li><strong>Select country</strong> — Choose your country to get the correct dimensions automatically</li>
          <li><strong>Adjust file size</strong> — Select the target file size (20KB, 50KB, or 100KB depending on requirements)</li>
          <li><strong>Download</strong> — Get your passport-ready photo instantly</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Common Mistakes to Avoid</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Wrong dimensions</strong> — Always check your country's specific requirements</li>
          <li><strong>Wrong file size</strong> — Some countries have strict maximum file sizes</li>
          <li><strong>Wrong background</strong> — White is required by most countries; avoid any patterns</li>
          <li><strong>Shadows</strong> — Use even lighting, avoid harsh shadows on face or background</li>
          <li><strong>Glasses</strong> — Remove if possible, or ensure no glare on lenses</li>
          <li><strong>Old photos</strong> — Use a photo taken within the last 6 months</li>
          <li><strong>Selfies</strong> — Avoid selfie distortion; use a tripod or have someone take the photo</li>
        </ul>

